# ─── Firebase / Google ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for Gemini AI API calls.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# The URL where this app is hosted (used for self-referential links, callbacks).
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"


# ─── Dahua DSS Pro ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# HOW CREDENTIALS WORK BY ENVIRONMENT:
#
#   LOCAL DEV  (npm run dev)
#     • Vite proxies /dahua/ → VITE_DAHUA_HOST via the dev server.
#     • Credentials are read by DahuaService.ts from VITE_DAHUA_* at build time.
#     • Create a .env.local file (gitignored) with the values below.
#
#   PRODUCTION  (Hostinger / any server running npm start)
#     • server.cjs serves dist/ and proxies /dahua/ server-side.
#     • Set DAHUA_HOST, DAHUA_USER, DAHUA_PASS as server env vars in Hostinger.
#     • Do NOT set VITE_DAHUA_PASS in production — it must not appear in the bundle.
#     • DahuaService.ts calls /api/dahua/login (server endpoint) in prod mode,
#       so the password stays on the server.

# --- For local dev only (.env.local) ---
VITE_DAHUA_HOST=https://your-dss-host.example.com
VITE_DAHUA_USER=api
VITE_DAHUA_PASS=your_dev_password_here

# --- For production (Hostinger environment variables panel) ---
# DAHUA_HOST=https://your-dss-host.example.com
# DAHUA_USER=api
# DAHUA_PASS=your_prod_password_here
